{"title":"2020 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A single bench section at a school event can hold either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> adults or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> children. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> bench sections are connected end to end, an equal number of adults and children seated together will occupy all the bench space. What is the least possible positive integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85cf31acc4d19289fd14d58e39c17cff9fe2b0e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N?$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d932ac55b336812b1b396ba7cd1c6b8865a1bbf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 27 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 36 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The least common multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, there must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> adults and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> children. The total number of benches is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/3801ae3699a24290ae6b5e38de35c29a85ee74c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{7}+\\frac{77}{11}=11+7=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"231\" height=\"38\" />.~taarunganesh\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> denote how many adults there are. Since the number of adults is equal to the number of children we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74c7133876b46ccafc1db1c3fecec5a669d42da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{7}+\\frac{x}{11}=N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"33\" />. Simplifying we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9ded2d2c586f6fc7af41703a18f3352fc6f31d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{18x}{77} = N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />\nSince both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> have to be positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> has to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af4b3f8897671e2879b10badf471e5deec8952e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$77$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196ad9aac61d9072daf2a321b8d08e711a1cd024.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" /> is our final answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have 1 Bench = 7 Adults = 11 Children, or\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91c3b15be2598e5ce5106982d008740f5e34a76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{11}{7}C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The minimum number of benches is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/912f0383398388d0324fa941517a1fa72c3e8d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = x(A + C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25980d178f07451b3093e0e104c43e09588358f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{77}{18}N = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />, so that the minimum value for x is the integer 18, or (B).\n</p><p>~PeterDoesPhysics\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Fast)\">Solution 4 (Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ratio of adults and children is 7:11 and the total amount of benches is the amount of adult and children combined which gives 7 + 11 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9f2c6d5aba65304489e7266c7a591f78ee175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />. We see that this is the smallest integer value.\n</p><p><br />\n~Twinotter\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Education, The Study of Everything\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GKTQO99CKPM\">https://youtu.be/GKTQO99CKPM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY\">https://youtu.be/JEjib74EmiY</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/w2_H96-yzk8\">https://youtu.be/w2_H96-yzk8</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=1616\">https://youtu.be/ZhAZ1oPe5Ds?t=1616</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span><